https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/homeowners-claim-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Commercial, Condo & HOA Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Roof & Hail Damage Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/roof-and-hail-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wind & Tornado Damage Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/wind-and-tornado-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Hurricane & Tropical Storm Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/hurricane-and-tropical-storm-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Water & Frozen Pipe Damage Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/water-damage-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Damage Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/fire-and-smoke-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/fallen-tree-damage-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Ice Dam & Winter Storm Appraisal","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/ice-dam-and-winter-storm-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance Estimate Review","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/insurance-estimate-review/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-services/umpire-services/"}}]},"knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Property claim valuation","Xactimate estimating","Fallen tree claims","Hurricane deductibles","Ice dam claims"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Connecticut Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/#webpage","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/","name":"Connecticut Insurance Appraisal FAQ | Costs & Timing","description":"Connecticut insurance appraisal FAQ grouped by topic: how appraisal works, costs, timing, state specifics and how we work with owners.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-17","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/living-room.webp","width":960,"height":640},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/#faq"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal FAQ","item":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/"}],"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is insurance appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is appraisal the same as arbitration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They’re similar but not identical. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal. It does not decide coverage or legal claims."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Under most policies, either you or the insurer can demand it in writing once you disagree on the amount of loss."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Connecticut law require an appraisal clause?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Connecticut’s standard fire policy, set out in state statute, contains an appraisal provision, and most homeowners and commercial forms include one. Read your own policy to confirm its wording."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an appraiser cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Arrangements vary: flat fees, hourly rates or a percentage of the increase. You pay your own appraiser and usually half the umpire. Get terms in writing first."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free consultation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Our first conversation is free, and we’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal is likely to be worth it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I recover appraisal costs from the insurer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually not under the policy itself, which typically makes each side bear its own appraiser. An attorney can advise whether any other recovery is available in your situation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does appraisal take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Simple residential claims often resolve in six to ten weeks after appraisers are named. Complex claims take longer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a deadline to demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some policies set one; many don’t say. Delay can create problems, and the suit-limitation period keeps running. Act promptly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does appraisal stop the clock on filing suit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not automatically. Protect the suit deadline separately and talk to an attorney if it is approaching."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who regulates insurers in Connecticut?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Connecticut Insurance Department, led by the Insurance Commissioner. It licenses insurers and adjusters and takes consumer complaints."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Connecticut FAIR Plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The state’s insurer of last resort for property owners who can’t find coverage in the regular market. Its policies have their own terms, including how disputes are handled."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Connecticut have a state wind pool?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Connecticut doesn’t operate a separate wind pool. Wind coverage comes through standard policies or the FAIR Plan, often with a hurricane deductible."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I think my insurer handled the claim unfairly?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Connecticut has an unfair insurance practices statute, CUIPA, that addresses unfair claim settlement practices, and such claims are sometimes pursued alongside CUTPA or common-law bad faith. These are legal questions; consult a Connecticut attorney. Appraisal does not decide them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you work for the insurance company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When we are your appraiser, you retain us. We also serve as neutral umpires on separate panels, and we disclose relationships on every file."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal or give legal advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I send for a first review?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your declarations page, the carrier’s full estimate, any letters from the carrier, your photos and any contractor estimate."}}],"@id":"https://connecticutinsuranceappraiser.com/ct-appraisal-faq/#faq"}]}</script>
</head>
