<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img class="phero-img" src="/assets/img/photos/living-room.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/living-room-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/living-room.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ</span></nav><p class="kicker kicker-light">Answers</p><h1>Connecticut Insurance Appraisal FAQ</h1><p class="phero-lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most, grouped by topic: the basics, costs, timing, Connecticut specifics and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/contact-ct-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="FAQ topics"><a href="#faq-0">The basics</a><a href="#faq-1">Costs and fees</a><a href="#faq-2">Timing and deadlines</a><a href="#faq-3">Connecticut specifics</a><a href="#faq-4">Working with us</a></nav><h2 id="faq-0">The basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>A process in most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers choose an umpire, and an award signed by two of the three sets the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They’re similar but not identical. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal. It does not decide coverage or legal claims.</p></div></details><details><summary>Who can demand appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Under most policies, either you or the insurer can demand it in writing once you disagree on the amount of loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Connecticut law require an appraisal clause?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Connecticut’s standard fire policy, set out in state statute, contains an appraisal provision, and most homeowners and commercial forms include one. Read your own policy to confirm its wording.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Costs and fees</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How much does an appraiser cost?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Arrangements vary: flat fees, hourly rates or a percentage of the increase. You pay your own appraiser and usually half the umpire. Get terms in writing first.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a free consultation?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Our first conversation is free, and we’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal is likely to be worth it.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I recover appraisal costs from the insurer?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not under the policy itself, which typically makes each side bear its own appraiser. An attorney can advise whether any other recovery is available in your situation.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Timing and deadlines</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Simple residential claims often resolve in six to ten weeks after appraisers are named. Complex claims take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a deadline to demand appraisal?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some policies set one; many don’t say. Delay can create problems, and the suit-limitation period keeps running. Act promptly.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal stop the clock on filing suit?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Not automatically. Protect the suit deadline separately and talk to an attorney if it is approaching.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Connecticut specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurers in Connecticut?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Connecticut Insurance Department, led by the Insurance Commissioner. It licenses insurers and adjusters and takes consumer complaints.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the Connecticut FAIR Plan?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The state’s insurer of last resort for property owners who can’t find coverage in the regular market. Its policies have their own terms, including how disputes are handled.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Connecticut have a state wind pool?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Connecticut doesn’t operate a separate wind pool. Wind coverage comes through standard policies or the FAIR Plan, often with a hurricane deductible.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I think my insurer handled the claim unfairly?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Connecticut has an unfair insurance practices statute, CUIPA, that addresses unfair claim settlement practices, and such claims are sometimes pursued alongside CUTPA or common-law bad faith. These are legal questions; consult a Connecticut attorney. Appraisal does not decide them.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you work for the insurance company?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>When we are your appraiser, you retain us. We also serve as neutral umpires on separate panels, and we disclose relationships on every file.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster or a law firm?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Neither. We provide appraisal, estimating and umpire services. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal or give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send for a first review?<svg class="ic chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Your declarations page, the carrier’s full estimate, any letters from the carrier, your photos and any contractor estimate.</p></div></details></div></article>
<aside class="side"><div class="side-sticky"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>A free, no-pressure conversation. We’ll say plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> +1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-coral btn-block" href="/contact-ct-appraiser/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><h2 class="side-t">Resources</h2><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/ct-appraisal-process/">Appraisal process guide<svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/ct-appraisal-faq/" aria-current="page">Appraisal FAQ<svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/ct-claim-glossary/">Claim glossary<svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/ct-claim-insights/">Claim insights<svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-strip"><div class="wrap cta-strip-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email. We’re happy to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/contact-ct-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
